OL,3,AInterest rates held but Bank signals
OL,4,Arise if energy prices stay high
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Bank of England has held interest
OL,7,Frates for the sixth time in a row but
OL,8,Fsaid they are likely to rise if high
OL,9,Fenergy prices caused by the conflict in
OL,10,Fthe Middle East continue.
OL,12,FThe main Bank rate has been kept at
OL,13,F3.75% despite an uptick in the rate of
OL,14,Finflation.
OL,16,FThe US-Israel war with Iran has
OL,17,Fdisrupted global energy supplies which
OL,18,Fhas led to a sharp increase in petrol
OL,19,Fand diesel prices.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
